    "title": "Report: Steve Kerr does not want 1 player on the Warriors - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Darryn Albert ,\n27 minutes ago Mar 20, 2022; San Francisco, California, USA; Golden State Warriors head coach Steve Kerr encourages his players during the fourth quarter against the San Antonio Spurs at Chase Center. Mandatory Credit: D. Ross Cameron-USA TODAY Sports Steve Kerr has one potential headache that he would rather avoid.\nThe Golden State Warriors head coach Kerr did not want the team to pursue a trade for Brooklyn Nets forward Michael Porter Jr. last February, Kevin O’Connor of The Ringer reported on Wednesday . O’Connor adds that there is also little reason to believe that Kerr wants Porter now.\nPorter, the former NBA lottery pick, is coming off a career year in which he averaged 24.2 points, 7.1 assists, and 3.0 assists per game. But this offseason, Porter has emerged as a potential trade candidate for a number of teams, including the Warriors.\nThat is because Porter is currently facing an uncertain future with the Nets. The 28-year-old forward is entering his final season under contract next year at $40.8 million and has yet to make much progress on an extension with the team. As a result, Porter has recently been the subject of trade rumors .\nGolden State needs some extra scoring punch with Jimmy Butler (torn ACL) set to miss a sizable chunk of next season. The Warriors also lost the likes of Pat Spencer and Quinten Post in free agency this summer and have yet to make any meaningful new additions.\nThat said, Porter remains an enigmatic player who is prone to poor shot selection, defensive lapses, and generally inconsistent play. It does not sound like that is an enigma which Kerr ( who recently returned to the Warriors on an interesting new deal ) wants to solve at this point.\nThe post Report: Steve Kerr does not want 1 player on the Warriors appeared first on Larry Brown Sports .",
    "summary": "Mandatory Credit: D. Ross Cameron-USA TODAY Sports Steve Kerr has one potential headache that he would rather avoid. The Golden State Warriors head coach Kerr did not want the team to pursue a trade for Brooklyn Nets forward Michael Porter Jr. last February, Kevin O’Connor of The Ringer reported on Wednesday . Golden State needs some extra scoring punch with Jimmy Butler (torn ACL) set to miss a sizable chunk of next season. The Warriors also lost the likes of Pat Spencer and Quinten Post in free agency this summer and have yet to make any meaningful new additions.",
